================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

The npm package `stratigraph` bundles no third-party code. Its runtime
dependencies are installed by npm from their own registries under their own
licences, and are listed in `package.json`.

The **Java extractor jar** — distributed as a GitHub release asset, fetched by
`stratigraph fetch-extractor`, and baked into the `ghcr.io` container image — is
a shaded ("fat") jar. It redistributes roughly 50 third-party artefacts inside
itself — including the Kotlin compiler, which is most of its size — so their
attribution notices travel with it:

  META-INF/NOTICE   — the merged attribution notices of every bundled component
  META-INF/LICENSE  — the merged licence texts

Both are assembled at build time by the maven-shade-plugin from the dependency
tree that actually produced the jar, rather than transcribed here, so they
cannot drift from what is really inside it. To read them:

  unzip -p stratigraph-java-extractor.jar META-INF/NOTICE

